This PR is 1 of 2 PRs for adding support to exclude requesting a review from employees who are on leave. This change updates the reviewer logic to support a different structure for the reviewer mapping, such that the keys are the full names of the reviewers and the object value contains their GitHub username in `codeReviewers` and `docsReviewers`, keeping the same functionality. 

<details>
  <summary>Example of the new mapping structure</summary>

```json
{
	"codeReviewers": {
		"fullname1": {
			"team": "Core",
			"owner": true, 
			"username": "gh-username1"
		}
	},
	"codeReviewersOmit": {
		"gh-username3": true
    },
	"docsReviewers": {
		"fullname4": {
			"team": "Core",
			"owner": true,
			"username": "gh-username4"
		}
	},	
	"docsReviewersOmit": {
		"gh-username6": true
    },
	"admins": [
		"gh-username7",
		"gh-username8"
	]
}
```

</details>

The purpose of this is the GitHub username is not provided when getting leave requests for reviewers, however, their full name is. In order to determine the Github username for the employee on leave, the mapping needs to contain the full name.

